Count the static counters, printing after each one is finished

E7 on the panel proves the whole ZALLOC phase completed, so the zone
registrations were never the problem.  The boot now stops at subsystem 9 rank 1,
and that group is exactly the 49 scalable_counter_static_init entries.

The earlier counter probe printed at the top of the function and destroyed the
one counter it was measuring: a printf drains through the log queue, and a full
queue calls counter_inc on log_queue_cnt_dropped_nomem, whose storage is being
initialised at that very moment.  Print at the end instead -- by then the counter
already points at its per-cpu slot, so the print cannot damage it.

  C0 .. C48   the last one printed is the last counter that finished
---
diff --git a/osfmk/kern/counter_common.c b/osfmk/kern/counter_common.c
--- a/osfmk/kern/counter_common.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/counter_common.c
@@ -73,2 +73,7 @@ scalable_counter_static_init(scalable_counter_t *counter)
 	os_atomic_store_wide(zpercpu_get(*counter), current_value, relaxed);
+	{
+		extern int printf(const char *, ...);
+		static uint32_t nio_ci;
+		printf("\nC%u", nio_ci++);
+	}
 	num_static_scalable_counters++;
